# Agent orientation (Orcan product)

**Orcan** is a Docker work-context orchestrator: workspaces, path parity, and
context packs. Agent CLIs are tools inside it; model routing is out of scope.

## Read order

1. Root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (= [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md)) — product and repository SoT.
2. [`docs/en/llms.txt`](../../docs/en/llms.txt) — public care / non-goals index.
3. [`docs/en/ai/project-context.md`](../../docs/en/ai/project-context.md) or [`change-map.md`](../../docs/en/change-map.md) only when needed.

In `orcan-dev`, honour the workspace context pack first. Use the `orcan` CLI
as the public interface; do not invent model routing, YAML user profiles,
deprecated Make-based user workflows, or speculative layers.
